blican nominee a substantial head start, and no general-election polls or expert ratings have yet been published to suggest a different picture.\n\nRecent headlines show Democrats making early campaign stops in the South, but there is no sign of a serious Democratic operation targeting Alabama itself. Republican primaries in the state have continued to favor Trump-backed candidates, underscoring the party's dominance. With no incumbent on the ballot and no polling to refine the estimate, the forecast rests on fundamentals and points to a comfortable Republican win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0924, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -15.0}]}